laurel 2011: the arm64 boot_args command line is 1024 bytes, as DarwinBoot (UniXNU) writes it (= negroni 0363).

The UEFI boot path (docs/laurel_sprout/uefi-boot.md) hands the kernel DARWIN_BOOT_ARGS from
external/UniXNU/drivers/DarwinBoot/DarwinBootPkg/Driver/BootArgs.h: CommandLine[1024], bootFlags at 0x470,
memSizeActual at 0x478 (the macOS arm64 layout). xnu-8796 has BOOT_LINE_LENGTH 608, so it would read bootFlags
at 0x2d0 and memSizeActual at 0x2d8 = bytes 612..627 of the command line (negroni: docs/notes.md section 35,
hw.memsize = boot-arg text, HFS+ journal sized from it, NULL write). With 1024 the fields are read where
DarwinBoot writes them. The topaz shim path (external/ios-topaz/tools/mkpayload.py, 608-byte header) does not
match this kernel any more; it is replaced by the UEFI path.

diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/boot.h
@@ -23,7 +23,9 @@
  * This value matches iBoot's IBOOT_MAX_ENV_VAR_DATA_SIZE.
  * There are no iBoot headers so have to duplicate it here for now.
  */
-#define BOOT_LINE_LENGTH        608
+/* laurel 2011 (= negroni 0363): DarwinBoot (UniXNU) writes the macOS arm64 layout, CommandLine[1024];
+ * with 608 the kernel reads memSizeActual from inside a long command line. */
+#define BOOT_LINE_LENGTH        1024
 
